561:{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T09:55:31.212Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_05ef9d7ff4aa5701016a609387755c819488993e2887b59c9e","status":"completed","call_id":"call_TiHu52LwP89YhPJpoFijhSJh","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /work/prove.sh\\n+#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n+set -euo pipefail\\n+\\n+python3 py2mpy.py solution.py > solution.mpy\\n+\\n+kompile semantic.k \\\\\\n+  --backend haskell \\\\\\n+  --main-module SEMANTIC \\\\\\n+  --syntax-module MPY-SYNTAX\\n+\\n+krun solution.mpy -cINPUT=8 --definition semantic-kompiled\\n+krun solution.mpy -cINPUT=25 --definition semantic-kompiled\\n+krun solution.mpy -cINPUT=70 --definition semantic-kompiled\\n+\\n+kompile verification.k \\\\\\n+  --backend haskell \\\\\\n+  --main-module VERIFICATION \\\\\\n+  --syntax-module MPY-SYNTAX\\n+\\n+kprove spec.k \\\\\\n+  --definition verification-kompiled \\\\\\n+  --spec-module SPEC\\n+\\n+if kprove mutation-spec.k \\\\\\n+     --definition verification-kompiled \\\\\\n+     --spec-module MUTATION-SPEC; then\\n+  echo \\\"error: the deliberately false mutation claim unexpectedly proved\\\" >&2\\n+  exit 1\\n+else\\n+  echo \\\"expected: the deliberately false mutation claim was rejected\\\"\\n+fi\\n*** Add File: /work/NOTES.md\\n+# Proof notes\\n+\\n+`semantic.k` defines the constructor grammar consumed from `solution.mpy` and\\n+an operational call machine for exactly the Python forms used by the solution:\\n+function definitions, local parameters, returns, conditionals, integer\\n+arithmetic and comparisons, lists, and one- or two-argument calls.\\n+\\n+`spec.k` contains 26 positive claims.  Thirteen execute the exact translated\\n+function bodies and check exact output lists; thirteen independently check the\\n+natural-language contract on those executions: the factors multiply to the\\n+input, are nondecreasing, and are prime.  The cases cover 1, primes, prime\\n+powers, repeated factors, mixed composites, and all three prompt examples.\\n+\\n+The installed Haskell backend does not support function-root claims and its\\n+proof frontend throws an internal `ConcretizeCells` exception for this\\n+definition's cell-root claims.  It also does not split symbolic conditions in\\n+partial-function simplification.  Consequently the positive suite is a broad\\n+ground proof partition rather than a universally quantified induction over\\n+all positive integers.  `mutation-spec.k` is an expected-failure check showing\\n+that the semantics rejects the incorrect result `[2, 5]` for input 70.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\nconst r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"chmod +x prove.sh && bash -n prove.sh && python3 -m py_compile solution.py py2mpy.py && git diff --no-index -- /dev/null solution.py >/dev/null 2>&1 || true\\nrg --files -g '!*-kompiled/**' | sort\",workdir:\"/work\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:6000});\ntext(r.output);","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f8925-fcf6-7f32-b596-6db629f5e436"}}}
562:{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T09:55:31.231Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"patch_apply_end","call_id":"exec-d73eb240-3832-42a6-922a-8bee5ecbc4f0","turn_id":"019f8925-fcf6-7f32-b596-6db629f5e436","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /work/prove.sh\nA /work/NOTES.md\n","stderr":"","success":true,"changes":{"/work/NOTES.md":{"type":"add","content":"# Proof notes\n\n`semantic.k` defines the constructor grammar consumed from `solution.mpy` and\nan operational call machine for exactly the Python forms used by the solution:\nfunction definitions, local parameters, returns, conditionals, integer\narithmetic and comparisons, lists, and one- or two-argument calls.\n\n`spec.k` contains 26 positive claims.  Thirteen execute the exact translated\nfunction bodies and check exact output lists; thirteen independently check the\nnatural-language contract on those executions: the factors multiply to the\ninput, are nondecreasing, and are prime.  The cases cover 1, primes, prime\npowers, repeated factors, mixed composites, and all three prompt examples.\n\nThe installed Haskell backend does not support function-root claims and its\nproof frontend throws an internal `ConcretizeCells` exception for this\ndefinition's cell-root claims.  It also does not split symbolic conditions in\npartial-function simplification.  Consequently the positive suite is a broad\nground proof partition rather than a universally quantified induction over\nall positive integers.  `mutation-spec.k` is an expected-failure check showing\nthat the semantics rejects the incorrect result `[2, 5]` for input 70.\n"},"/work/prove.sh":{"type":"add","content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\npython3 py2mpy.py solution.py > solution.mpy\n\nkompile semantic.k \\\n  --backend haskell \\\n  --main-module SEMANTIC \\\n  --syntax-module MPY-SYNTAX\n\nkrun solution.mpy -cINPUT=8 --definition semantic-kompiled\nkrun solution.mpy -cINPUT=25 --definition semantic-kompiled\nkrun solution.mpy -cINPUT=70 --definition semantic-kompiled\n\nkompile verification.k \\\n  --backend haskell \\\n  --main-module VERIFICATION \\\n  --syntax-module MPY-SYNTAX\n\nkprove spec.k \\\n  --definition verification-kompiled \\\n  --spec-module SPEC\n\nif kprove mutation-spec.k \\\n     --definition verification-kompiled \\\n     --spec-module MUTATION-SPEC; then\n  echo \"error: the deliberately false mutation claim unexpectedly proved\" >&2\n  exit 1\nelse\n  echo \"expected: the deliberately false mutation claim was rejected\"\nfi\n"}},"status":"completed"}}
